---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Subscribe from '../components/Subscribe.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="A photograph a week, alternating between Sean Ryan and a rotating cast of guest photographers."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="prose__title">About</h1>

    <p>
      Perch is a photo journal that alternates. One week the photograph is mine.
      The next it belongs to someone else — a friend, another photographer,
      whoever has been carrying a camera lately.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every photograph comes with a short written piece underneath, and every
      guest keeps their own byline. Not a response exactly — just the next frame
      in a conversation that happens to be made of pictures instead of
      sentences. The writing matters as much as the picture: a paragraph or two
      about where it came from, what they were after, what they missed.
    </p>

    <div class="ledger">
      <p class="ledger__row">
        <span class="ledger__name">Sean Ryan</span>
        <span class="ledger__weeks">Odd weeks</span>
      </p>
      <p class="ledger__row">
        <span class="ledger__name">A guest</span>
        <span class="ledger__weeks">Even weeks</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="prose__heading">What to expect</h2>

    <p>
      Subscribe and each entry arrives by email when it goes up — one
      photograph, a few words, nothing else. No fixed schedule, no promotions,
      no filler. Everything stays on the site too: scroll the homepage and the
      whole run is there, newest first, and every entry has its own page so a
      single photograph can be shared on its own.
    </p>

    <p>
      There are no comments, no likes, no follower counts, and no algorithm
      deciding who sees what. People subscribe and the photograph arrives. The
      restraint is the point.
    </p>

    <h2 class="prose__heading">The rules, such as they are</h2>

    <ul class="rules">
      <li>One photograph. Not a set, not a gallery — one.</li>
      <li>Roughly weekly. Miss a week; the thing survives.</li>
      <li>No theme, no brief, no assignment. Shoot what you notice.</li>
      <li>Phone pictures count.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="prose__heading">Guests</h2>

    <p>
      Guest weeks are by invitation, and the invitation is usually just a text
      message. If you have a photograph you have been meaning to show someone,
      that is the whole qualification. Send the picture at full size and a few
      sentences about it; the byline stays yours.
    </p>

    <p class="prose__back"><a href="/">&larr; Read the journal</a></p>
  </article>

  <Subscribe />
</Base>
